# Configuration for the cpufreq service (openrc/init.d/cpufreq).
#
# Why this exists: the base config sets CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_USERSPACE,
# and under the userspace governor nothing drives the clocks at boot — the
# box idles low until a governor is written. Pinning it here (design D4)
# keeps CONFIG_CPU_FREQ on, which CPU_THERMAL needs, while giving the box
# predictable clocks.
#
# OpenRC auto-sources this file because the service is named "cpufreq";
# no consumer writes a source line for it.
GOVERNOR="performance"
